      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence defines cross-modal matching as a general “ability to connect information from one sense with corresponding information from another sense.” The packet specifically discusses infants’ audio-visual matching of speech (e.g., matching auditory and visual speech/syllables), but it does not explicitly support this broader, general “ability to connect information” framing.",
        "The second sentence’s emphasis on sequential (one after the other) vs simultaneous presentation is supported by the packet (it discusses that sequential presentation is necessary to rule out matching based on audio-visual synchrony)."
